      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:johnconst.penitence.budge:1-119",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲱ ⲛⲁⲓⲁⲧϥ ⲛⲟⲩϩⲏⲕⲉ ⲛⲣⲉϥϣⲡϩⲙⲟⲧ · ⲛⲣⲙⲣⲁϣ ⲛⲃⲁⲗϩⲏⲧ ϫⲉϥⲛⲁⲉⲓ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ϩⲛⲧⲙⲛⲧϩⲏⲕⲉ ⲙⲡⲉⲓⲕⲟⲥⲙⲟⲥ · ⲛⲥⲉϫⲓⲧϥ ⲉⲩⲙⲛⲧⲣⲙⲙⲁⲟ ⲛ**ⲁⲧⲟⲩⲱ** ·",
      "english": "And blessed is the poor man who giveth thanks, and who is meek and gentle, for he shall go forth from the poverty of this world, and shall receive riches which are neverending.",
      "source": "Encomium on Victor part 3",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pscelestinus.encomium.budge:56-103",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲱ ⲛⲉⲕⲁⲛⲱⲙⲓⲁ ϩⲛϩⲉⲛⲙⲛⲧϣⲁⲛϩⲧⲏϥ ⲉϩⲟⲩⲛ ⲉⲛϩⲏⲕⲉ · ϫⲉⲕⲁⲥ ⲉⲕⲛⲁⲡⲟⲗⲁⲩⲉ ⲙⲙⲟⲕ ϩⲛⲧⲙⲛⲧⲣⲙⲙⲁⲟ ⲛ**ⲁⲧⲟⲩⲱ** ·",
      "english": "Do thou redeem thy sins by charity, and thy lawlessness by gifts of alms to the poor, in order that thou mayest have enjoyment in the riches which do not come to an end.",
      "source": "Encomium on Victor part 2",
